    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Splits time series into trend, seasonal and residual components (additive or multiplicative) with seasonally adjusted values, seasonal indices and strength measures.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Time Series",
    "tags": [
        "seasonality",
        "decomposition",
        "trend",
        "seasonally adjusted",
        "time series",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Explains a time series rather than forecasting it: how much is **trend**, how much is the **seasonal** pattern that repeats every year (or week), and what is left over (**residual**: promotions, one-offs, noise).\n\n- Classical decomposition with a centred moving average, **additive** (seasonal effect in units) or **multiplicative** (seasonal effect in %)\n- **Seasonally adjusted** values: the series with the seasonal pattern removed, so month-on-month changes mean something\n- **Seasonal indices** per season (January to December, Q1 to Q4, Monday to Sunday) with the effect versus trend\n- Per series: **seasonality strength** and **trend strength** (0 to 1), peak and trough season, trend change over the period, residual spread\n- Several series at once (per category, store, region); duplicate dates are summed and missing periods interpolated (and flagged); the trend can be extended to the ends of the series\n\nNeeds at least two full seasons per series. Complements Omniscope's Time Series Forecast block: decompose to understand, forecast to plan.",
